  "id": "5774b118-c5f1-5793-b8d8-77ef33e8c88d",
  "slug": "strawberry-snow-cone-recipe-11963034",
  "name": "Strawberry Snow Cone",
  "recipe_type": "dessert",
  "brief_description": "A strawberry snow cone is the perfect way to cool down on a warm day, combining the refreshing crunch of ice with the sweet, fruity flavor of fresh strawberries. This simple homemade version uses real ingredients to create a naturally vibrant syrup that tastes far better than store-bought options. With just a few steps, you can turn juicy strawberries into a delicious topping that transforms plain crushed ice into a bright, refreshing treat everyone will enjoy.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Combine strawberries, sugar, and water in a saucepan. Heat over medium heat, stirring occasionally, until strawberries soften and the sugar dissolves, about 5 to 7 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Let mixture cool slightly, then blend it until smooth. If you prefer a smoother syrup, strain it through a fine mesh sieve to remove seeds."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Refrigerate the syrup until it's cold."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Fill a cup or cone with crushed ice and drizzle the strawberry syrup generously. Recipe excerpted from Route 66 Recipes: A Culinary Cruise Along the Mother Road , reprinted with permission from Arcadia Publishing."
    }
  ],
